      }
    },
    {
      "title": "How It Works",
      "content": "The miniCTX benchmark consists of 762 theorems from six projects, each associated with a context that can span tens of thousands of tokens. <strong>File-tuning</strong> is a method that fine-tunes language models on human-written (state, context, tactic) triples to generate tactics based on the current context and proof state. <strong>Premise selection</strong> is used to extract relevant premises from imported files within the same repository.",
