    {
      "title": "The Results",
      "content": "The results show that <strong>context-dependent methods improve theorem proving</strong> dramatically. The file-tuned model improves over traditional state-tactic models, especially in problems that have dependencies on context. <strong>Premise selection</strong> improves performance on high cross-file dependency splits, but may interfere with in-file context.",
